  {
    "@id": "https://wiren301.github.io/iso27001-skos-taxonomy/27002/control/5.21",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Manage supply chain dangers."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "https://wiren301.github.io/iso27001-skos-taxonomy/27001/control/A.5.21"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "ICT supply chain risks for an organization can stem from: a) purchase or use of counterfeit hardware or hardware with embedded malware; b) vulnerabilities in software components or services provided to the organization, whether obtained through supplier or other sources; c) outsourced application development; d) disclosure or leakage of business- or customer-sensitive information by supply chain participants; e) intentional or unintentional introduction of malware or backdoors or unauthorized features into delivered items."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://wiren301.github.io/iso27001-skos-taxonomy/27002/ControlsScheme"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
      {
        "@value": "5.21"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Assess pre-acquisition."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Managing information security in the information and communication technology (ICT) supply chain"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Sustain relationship security."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://wiren301.github.io/iso27001-skos-taxonomy/27001/control/A.8.10",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Purge old data."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://wiren301.github.io/iso27001-skos-taxonomy/27001/AnnexAScheme"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
      {
        "@value": "A.8.10"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Information deletion"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://wiren301.github.io/iso27001-skos-taxonomy/27002/control/8.18",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Restrict admin tools."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "https://wiren301.github.io/iso27001-skos-taxonomy/27001/control/A.8.18"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Most information systems have one or more utility programs that can be capable of overriding system and application controls, for example diagnostics, patching, antivirus, disk defragmenters, debuggers, backup and network tools."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://wiren301.github.io/iso27001-skos-taxonomy/27002/ControlsScheme"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
      {
        "@value": "8.18"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Limit to authorized staff."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Use of privileged utility programs"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Prevent control bypass."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://wiren301.github.io/iso27001-skos-taxonomy/27000/term/3.72",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "danger mitigation"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://wiren301.github.io/iso27001-skos-taxonomy/27000/VocabularyScheme"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
      {
        "@value": "3.72"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Risk treatment can involve: — avoiding the risk by deciding not to start or continue with the activity that gives rise to the risk; — taking or increasing risk in order to pursue an opportunity; — removing the risk source; — changing the likelihood (3.40); — changing the consequences (3.12); — sharing the risk with another party or parties (including contracts and risk financing); — retaining the risk by informed choice. | Risk treatments that deal with negative consequences are sometimes referred to as \"risk mitigation\", \"risk elimination\", \"risk prevention\" and \"risk reduction\". | Risk treatment can create new risks or modify existing risks."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "risk treatment"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://wiren301.github.io/iso27001-skos-taxonomy/27000/term/3.74",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "harm potential"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://wiren301.github.io/iso27001-skos-taxonomy/27000/VocabularyScheme"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
      {
        "@value": "3.74"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "threat"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://wiren301.github.io/iso27001-skos-taxonomy/27001/control/A.6.5",
    "@type": [
